      "content": "thanks for clarifying that. one thing that's bothering me though is the idea of \"uncertainty\" making things feel so messy and unreliable. it almost feels like there's some weird kind of error or noise messing with the numbers so they don't align perfectly. is there a way to account for that kind of randomness so it doesn't feel so chaotic in the final results?",
